  "major": "Counseling Psychology",
  "notes": "With Emphasis in Marriage and Family Therapy, Professional Clinical Counseling, and Depth Psychology. Prepares for LMFT and LPCC licensure in California. Two-and-a-half year program (10 quarters). Professional Skills Development I series (CP 565 > CP 566 > CP 567 > CP 568) must be taken in sequential order as prerequisites to enter the Professional Skills Development II series and CP 610 Clinical Practice I. Comprehensive Oral Examination (CP 612E, 0 units) in Second Year Spring; Comprehensive Written Examination (CP 615E, 0 units) in Third Year Winter. Counseling Psychology classes take place in three-day sessions occurring three times in each of the fall, winter, and spring quarters; seven-day summer session each of the first two years.",
